,"node_id":"U_kgDOESNhYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287531360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase","html_url":"https://github.com/Roger-LegalEase","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean/actions/runs/34445997139/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean/actions/runs/34445997139/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean/check-suites/93312106875","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean/actions/runs/34445997139/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean/actions/runs/34445997139/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean/actions/runs/34445997139/rerun","previous_attempt_url":null,"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean/actions/workflows/347286543","head_commit":{"id":"8a139cc8f0f12d7af847b505154fc298f513797b","tree_id":"8f705a96b4587cd8d877013b3927594c8f2b20e4","message":"Forty families count the source's own scanned pages as appearances their build flattened\n\nVF31 passed ar-nonconviction-seal-set on all fifteen obligations with all nine\ncounters measured -- FAIL_REPAIR_REQUIRED to BUILT_RASTER_PENDING, and it owes a\ncentral raster -- and failed its sibling ar-cs-possession-seal-set on ARTIFACTS for a\ncounter that is not what it says it is.\n\nar-cs-possession's petitions publish flattenedWidgetAppearancesReadFromOutputBytes:\n125. The bytes carry 41. The extra 84 are the ACIC petition's own SCANNED PAGE IMAGES,\ncounted as appearances this build added. VF31 confirmed 41 three ways: the newer\nreading module, direct XObject definition and Do-invocation counts, and the source's\nown acroFieldCount of 41. The same file also publishes addedGlyphsReadFromOutputBytes\n0 on all four fixtures with \"Zero by construction, not by measurement\", where the bytes\ncarry 124, 214, 72 and 80 -- and the family's own rendered-artifacts.json publishes\nexactly those.\n\nThe cause is in pdf-flattened-widgets.mjs. Its pattern matches\n`q <cm>... /<name> Do`, and its comment is right that the multiple cm matters. What it\ndoes not do is check the NAME: `\\/(\\S+)\\s+Do` matches any XObject drawn that way, and a\nscanned page image is drawn exactly that way.\n\nThat module has 72 callers, so I measured the blast radius rather than changing it on\none family's evidence. Across every family with delivered fixtures:\n\n  144  families measured\n   40  publish an inflated count\n  494  phantom appearances in total\n  104  families where the count is already true\n\n  +168  ar-cs-possession-seal-set          +26  il-exp-nonconv-set\n   +20  each of eight more Illinois families and wv-acc-treatment-job-readiness-set\n    +8  wv-conv-multiple-misdemeanors-set, and the rest smaller\n\nAn overcount is not by itself a page defect -- the extra placements are the source's\nown images, correctly drawn. What is wrong is a counter reporting them as ink the\nbuild flattened, and this counter is not idle: West Virginia's read established that\nthe raw appearance count would let empty appearances certify a packet that drew\nnothing, which is why invisibleWrites there sums only the carrying-text subset.\n\nTHE FIX IS ONE PREDICATE -- accept only the names the finalizer gives its own output,\n/FlatWidget-N and /ExactFactOverlay-N -- AND I AM NOT APPLYING IT YET. Six lanes are\nrunning against these builders right now, and a shared module that changes under a\nlane mid-measurement produces a return whose numbers cannot be reconciled with its own\nmethod. That is the discipline I have been asking lanes to observe and it applies to\nme. It goes in when they are back, and until then the forty families' published counts\nare stale rather than wrong-and-unrecorded.\n\nVF31 also found what the artifacts get right where the prose does not: both Arkansas\nfamilies' instructions say the packet \"writes nothing\" in the order's decree, and both\nwrite the participant's legal name there -- correctly typeset on the rule, which VF31\nrendered and read. The artifact is right and the prose is wrong, so the fix is in prose\nand never in the PDF. And it recorded that FIX137's own row understates its own\nmeasurement: the row says 0 appearances not placed at their own source widget, the\ndelivered report says 1, and running FIX137's module returns 1 -- a 12-byte stream\nthat draws nothing on a page that renders pixel-identical to source.\n\nTerminal holds at 191 of 346; every step exit 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W3FAJNotS5DdvyJS1khjid","timestamp":"2026-09-10T06:36:44Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1248656766,"node_id":"R_kgDOSmz9fg","name":"legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","full_name":"Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","private":false,"o